UID:5f2f21bc5a1cb309abd7d5c5fbf5c0b4dc2ad392@phillyfamily.com
DTSTAMP:20261119T191548Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261229T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261229T200000
SUMMARY:Celebrating Ujamaa: Kwanzaa Quizzo and Evening Bazaar
LOCATION:Franklin Square\, 200 N 6th St\, Philadelphia\, PA 19106
DESCRIPTION:Inspired by Kwanzaa’s fourth principle\, Ujamaa\, which empha
 sizes cooperative economics and supporting Black-owned businesses\, the Af
 rican American Museum in Philadelphia is hosting a family-friendly holiday
  market featuring Black-owned vendors from across the region. Visitors can
  shop for unique gifts\, known as Zawadi in Swahili\, while supporting loc
 al businesses. The event will also feature a Kwanzaa-themed Quizzo\, music
 \, and additional activities for the whole family.\n\nEvent website: https
 ://historicphiladelphia.org/events/kwanzaa-celebration/\n\nListing: https:
 //phillyfamily.com/event/celebrating-ujamaa-kwanzaa-quizzo-and-evening-baz
 aar/
URL:https://historicphiladelphia.org/events/kwanzaa-celebration/
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts,Community Event,Fall Fun,Family Event,Free,Hanukka
 h/Chanukkah,Kid Event
END:VEVENT
