SUMMARY:(Daily) Botany of Nations at The Academy of Natural Sciences
LOCATION:The Academy of Natural Sciences\, 1900 Benjamin Franklin Pkwy\, Ph
 iladelphia\, PA 19103
DESCRIPTION:From March 28\, 2026 to February 14\, 2027\, Botany of Nations 
 is a groundbreaking exhibition that offers a culturally layered\, new pers
 pective on the legendary Lewis and Clark Corps of Discovery\, co-curated w
 ith ethnobotanist and author Enrique Salmón\, PhD\, and developed with co
 ntributions from Indigenous cultural historians. Centering the voices of N
 ative Nations who have protected and cared for these lands for thousands o
 f years\, the exhibition presents plants as portals to Indigenous…\n\nEv
 ent website: https://ansp.org/\n\nListing: https://phillyfamily.com/event/
 daily-botany-of-nations-at-the-academy-of-natural-sciences/2027-01-23/
